#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The B<wcscat> function is the wide-character equivalent of the B<strcat> "
#| "function. It copies the wide-character string pointed to by I<src>, "
#| "including the terminating L'\\e0' character, to the end of the wide-"
#| "character string pointed to by I<dest>."
msgid ""
"The B<wcscat>()  function is the wide-character equivalent of the "
"B<strcat>(3)  function.  It copies the wide-character string pointed to by "
"I<src>, including the terminating null wide character "
"(L\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq]), to the end of the wide-character string pointed to "
"by I<dest>."
msgstr ""
"La función B<wcscat> es el equivalente de caracteres anchos de la función "
"B<strcat>. Copia la cadena de caracteres anchos apuntada por I<src>, "
"incluyendo el carácter de terminación L'\\e0' al final de la cadena de "
"caracteres anchos I<dest>."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The strings may not overlap."
msgstr "Las cadenas no se pueden solapar."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The programmer must ensure that there is room for at least "
"I<wcslen(dest)>+I<wcslen(src)>+1 wide characters at I<dest>."
msgstr ""
"El programador tiene que asegurarse de que hay espacio para al menos "
"I<wcslen(dest)>+I<wcslen(src)>+1 caracteres anchos en I<dest>."

#. type: SH
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "RETURN VALUE"
msgstr "VALOR DEVUELTO"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "B<wcscat>()  returns I<dest>."
msgstr "B<wscat>() devuelve I<dest>."

